statementMd:
You are given a quantum oracle - an operation on $*N* + 1$ qubits which implements a function ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/ca923da5e61e139eb5596a3b9e34cc7ef42d1433.png). You are guaranteed that the function $*f*$ implemented by the oracle can be represented in the following form (oracle from problem D2):

![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/b2eb3d0e407b200708fe5e4dc65e777bc2c88984.png)

Here ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/b27ec8b8056386de828da0df174348afa7d29512.png) (a vector of $*N*$ integers, each of which can be 0 or 1), and ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/823bed8a1021f190960cf0b721fad709b7641d0e.png) is a vector of $*N*$ 1s.

Your task is to reconstruct the array ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/71fa108edb785ca9f729fa3cd5ad18556dd682e4.png) which could produce the given oracle. Your code is allowed to call the given oracle only once.

You have to implement an operation which takes the following inputs:

- an integer $*N*$ - the number of qubits in the oracle input ($1 ≤ *N* ≤ 8$),
- an oracle $*Uf*$, implemented as an operation with signature `((Qubit[], Qubit) => ())`, i.e., an operation which takes as input an array of qubits and an output qubit and has no output.

The return of your operation is an array of integers of length $*N*$, each of them 0 or 1.

Note that in this problem we're comparing the oracle generated by your return to the oracle $*Uf*$, instead of comparing your return to the (hidden) value of ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/71fa108edb785ca9f729fa3cd5ad18556dd682e4.png) used to generate $*Uf*$. This means that any kind of incorrect return results in "Runtime Error" verdict, as well as actual runtime errors like releasing qubits in non-zero state.

Your code should have the following signature:

```
namespace Solution {
    open Microsoft.Quantum.Primitive;
    open Microsoft.Quantum.Canon;

    operation Solve (N : Int, Uf : ((Qubit[], Qubit) => ())) : Int[]
    {
        body
        {
            // your code here
        }
    }
}
```

statementZhMd:
你获得了一个量子 oracle——一个作用于 $*N* + 1$ 个量子比特、实现函数 ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/ca923da5e61e139eb5596a3b9e34cc7ef42d1433.png) 的操作。保证该 oracle 实现的函数 $*f*$ 可以表示为以下形式（来自问题 D2 的 oracle）：

![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/b2eb3d0e407b200708fe5e4dc65e777bc2c88984.png)

其中，![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/b27ec8b8056386de828da0df174348afa7d29512.png) 是一个包含 $*N*$ 个整数的向量，其中每个整数都可以是 0 或 1；而 ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/823bed8a1021f190960cf0b721fad709b7641d0e.png) 是一个由 $*N*$ 个 1 组成的向量。

你的任务是重构数组 ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/71fa108edb785ca9f729fa3cd5ad18556dd682e4.png)，使其能够生成给定的 oracle。你的代码只能调用给定的 oracle 一次。

你需要实现一个操作，该操作接受以下输入：

- 一个整数 $*N*$——oracle 输入中的量子比特数量（$1 ≤ *N* ≤ 8$）；
- 一个 oracle $*Uf*$，其实现是一个签名为 `((Qubit[], Qubit) => ())` 的操作，即该操作接收一个量子比特数组和一个输出量子比特作为输入，且没有输出。

你的操作应返回一个长度为 $*N*$ 的整数数组，其中每个元素都是 0 或 1。

请注意，在本题中，我们比较的是根据你的返回值生成的 oracle 与 oracle $*Uf*$，而不是将你的返回值与用于生成 $*Uf*$ 的（隐藏的）![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/71fa108edb785ca9f729fa3cd5ad18556dd682e4.png) 进行比较。这意味着任何形式的错误返回都会得到“Runtime Error”判定，和释放处于非零状态的量子比特等实际运行时错误一样。

